            <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold text-ink mb-4">CNG Price in Delhi — IGL's Network, the National Benchmark</h3>
            <p class="text-body mb-6">
              The <strong>CNG price in Delhi today</strong> is the number most other North Indian cities are measured against. Delhi's CNG is sold by Indraprastha Gas Limited (IGL), which also serves Noida, Ghaziabad, Gurugram, Faridabad and a wide swathe of the NCR. IGL's pricing reflects its mix of domestic APM gas and imported LNG, plus compression costs at its station network, before central excise and Delhi's state VAT are applied. Because Delhi's overall fuel-tax structure is moderate by national standards — the same low-VAT advantage that keeps its petrol cheap relative to Mumbai — CNG here typically lands mid-pack nationally, cheaper than high-tax states but not the cheapest in India. For NCR commuters, the practical point is that the <strong>CNG price in Noida</strong> ({noidaCng ?? "on the IGL network"}) and the <strong>CNG price in Ghaziabad</strong> ({ghaziabadCng ?? "on the IGL network"}) are set by the same IGL network as Delhi and usually track within a narrow band — there's no meaningful cross-border arbitrage inside the NCR. <a href="/cng-price-in-delhi/" class="text-primary hover:underline font-semibold">Delhi CNG price page →</a>
            </p>

            <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold text-ink mb-4">CNG Price in Mumbai — MGL's Network Across the Metro</h3>
            <p class="text-body mb-6">
              The <strong>CNG price in Mumbai today</strong> ({mumbaiCng ?? "set by MGL"}) is set by Mahanagar Gas Limited (MGL), which covers Mumbai, Thane, Navi Mumbai and surrounding areas. MGL's CNG pricing follows the same four-layer structure — gas cost, compression, margin, taxes — but Maharashtra's tax stack applies on top, the same structure that makes the state's petrol among India's most expensive. MGL has one of the country's most mature CNG networks, which keeps compression and distribution costs relatively efficient per kg, but the state VAT layer still shows up in the final number. Mumbai's rate typically sits above Delhi's and serves as a reference point for the western corridor. <a href="/cng-price-in-mumbai/" class="text-primary hover:underline font-semibold">Mumbai CNG price page →</a>
            </p>

            <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold text-ink mb-4">CNG Price in Bangalore — Expanding Network, Growing Supply</h3>
            <p class="text-body mb-6">
              The <strong>CNG price in Bangalore today</strong> ({bangaloreCng ?? "set by the local distributor"}) reflects a network that has been scaling up over the past few years. Bangalore's CNG infrastructure is newer than Delhi's or Mumbai's, which means the fixed costs of building out compressor stations are spread across a still-growing volume — a factor that can keep per-kg rates slightly higher than in fully mature networks. Karnataka's tax structure applies on top of the gas cost, and the state's relatively high sales-tax environment (the same one behind its petrol prices) flows through to CNG where VAT is charged. Availability, more than price, has historically been Bangalore's CNG constraint — but the network keeps expanding, and the rate today is worth comparing against petrol if you're weighing a conversion. <a href="/cng-price-in-bangalore/" class="text-primary hover:underline font-semibold">Bangalore CNG price page →</a>
            </p>

            <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold text-ink mb-4">CNG Price in Pune, Kolkata & Hyderabad</h3>
            <p class="text-body mb-6">
              Pune's CNG ({puneCng ?? "set by the local distributor"} per kg today) sits on the Maharashtra network — same state tax structure as Mumbai, with distribution costs that reflect Pune's position on the pipeline grid. Kolkata's rate ({kolkataCng ?? "set by the local distributor"} per kg) is set through West Bengal's licensed distributors; the state's VAT and cess structure that makes its petrol expensive also applies to CNG, which keeps Kolkata's per-kg rate toward the higher end of the eastern grid. Hyderabad ({hyderabadCng ?? "set by the local distributor"} per kg today) operates in Telangana's high-tax environment — the same 35%+ VAT regime behind India's most expensive petrol — and while CNG's percentage-based excise and different gas-cost base mean the gap doesn't mirror petrol exactly, the state's tax posture does push Hyderabad's CNG above many peers. <a href="/cng-price-in-hyderabad/" class="text-primary hover:underline font-semibold">Hyderabad CNG page →</a> · <a href="/cng-price-in-kolkata/" class="text-primary hover:underline font-semibold">Kolkata CNG page →</a> · <a href="/cng-price-in-pune/" class="text-primary hover:underline font-semibold">Pune CNG page →</a>
            </p>

            <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold text-ink mb-4">CNG Price in Ahmedabad, Jaipur, Chennai & Indore</h3>
            <p class="text-body mb-6">
              Ahmedabad ({ahmedabadCng ?? "set by Gujarat Gas"}) benefits from Gujarat's position as India's gas heartland — Gujarat Gas is one of the largest CGD networks in the country, and the state's proximity to pipeline infrastructure and historically moderate tax posture keep the per-kg rate competitive. Jaipur's CNG ({jaipurCng ?? "set by the local distributor"} per kg today) is served through Rajasthan's expanding network; the state's high petrol VAT doesn't map one-to-one onto CNG, but any state levies that apply do show up in the final rate. Chennai ({chennaiCng ?? "set by the local distributor"} per kg) has a smaller CNG footprint than Delhi or Mumbai — Tamil Nadu's CNG network is still developing relative to its petrol and diesel demand — and the state's flat-plus-percentage tax structure shapes whatever rate local distributors post. Indore ({indoreCng ?? "set by the local distributor"} per kg) sits in Madhya Pradesh's Central India grid, where CNG coverage is growing but still thinner than the western metros. <a href="/cng-price-in-jaipur/" class="text-primary hover:underline font-semibold">Jaipur →</a> · <a href="/cng-price-in-ahmedabad/" class="text-primary hover:underline font-semibold">Ahmedabad →</a> · <a href="/cng-price-in-chennai/" class="text-primary hover:underline font-semibold">Chennai →</a> · <a href="/cng-price-in-indore/" class="text-primary hover:underline font-semibold">Indore →</a>
            </p>

            <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold text-ink mb-4">CNG Price in Chandigarh, Lucknow, Ghaziabad & Noida</h3>
